ate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Weaknesses: relatively weak memory for numbers, regarded as pretentious. So strengths: reliability (conscientious), stress resilience, technical (weather, computer). Concerns: memory for numbers (attention/accuracy), pretentious (crew cooperation).\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, puts concern for others above everything. Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, crew cooperation (concern for others). Concerns: communication, egocentric, lack of development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weaknesses: regarded as know-it-all, considered moody. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: crew cooperation (know-it-all, moody).\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate C has good decision making, calm, concern for others, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious. Candidate D has strong technical and responsibility, but moody and know-it-all may affect crew. Candidate B is reliable and stress resilient, but weak memory for numbers could be safety-critical. Candidate A has technical strengths but unfriendly.\n\nWhich candidate balances? Perhaps Candidate D: strong responsibility, concentration, problem solving, adaptability, but moody and know-it-all could be mitigated? Candidate C's communication difficulty is a big issue for cockpit. Candidate B's memory for numbers is also safety-critical. Candidate A's unfriendly may affect crew.\n\nThus I might lean toward Candidate D as best overall, despite concerns.\n\nMake contribution: state recommendation for Candidate D, reference that we have discussed strengths like responsibility, concentration, problem solving, and concerns like moody/know-it-all, and argue that strengths outweigh concerns relative to others.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the candidate facts we have, I propose...\"\n\nOk.\n\nWe need METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
